  "description": "HUJWEQ crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H189 Cu3 Ho9 O55 P6 1-,C8 H12 Cu1 N4 1+. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Ho1B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.413-4.254 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.99-122.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu(MeCN)4][Cu3Ho9(μ3-OH)7(O3PtBu)6(O2CtBu)15]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 7 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
